title: What a save now says about hides, for Jeff cold.
pid: 2bb62f95-4b22-41c3-9a31-456bc2f7f62b
body: |2-
  After each save, Emacs's echo area (and Neovim's notice) lists what the
  save hid from or stopped hiding from a note that follows another, as
  "Hides 'A detail' from 'My copy of Fred's note', as content of 'Fred's
  note'." or "Stops hiding ..."; and when a child you took out of such a
  note hid nothing, it says why, as "Hides nothing: 'X' left 'My copy',
  but it is no content of 'Fred's note', nor overrides any."
